// Apologizing (design doc: Harm & forgiveness): the player said "I'm sorry about before."
// owes_apology - something between you is still unforgiven; apology_too_soon - they need time first
// (a Cranky pony a day, a Grudge Holder longer); apology_believed - a sorry still means something
// (each one counts for less, and cruelty for less again). "~ forgive" is the repair.
//
// PLACEHOLDER LINES - a scaffold showing the shape; every line here is meant to be rewritten.


=== nothing_to_forgive
start: apology
when: not owes_apology
{pony}: Sorry? For what? We're fine, silly.

=== not_yet
start: apology
weight: 100
when: owes_apology, apology_too_soon
{pony}: Not now. I need some time to myself.
    or: ...I heard you. Just - give me a little while, okay?

=== not_believed
start: apology
weight: 100
when: owes_apology, not apology_too_soon, not apology_believed
{pony}: You keep saying that. I don't think I believe you anymore.

=== forgiven
start: apology
when: owes_apology, not apology_too_soon, apology_believed
{pony}: ...Okay. Thank you for saying it. Let's put it behind us.
~ forgive

=== forgiven_gentle
start: apology
weight: 3
when: owes_apology, not apology_too_soon, apology_believed, personality(gentle)
{pony}: Oh, of course I forgive you! Please don't worry about it.
~ forgive

=== forgiven_cranky
start: apology
weight: 3
when: owes_apology, not apology_too_soon, apology_believed, personality(cranky)
{pony}: Hmph. ...Fine. Apology accepted. Don't make a habit of it.
~ forgive
